{"title":"Career Roadmap: Cryptography Assistant","role":"Cryptography Assistant","summary":"A Cryptography Assistant supports the design, implementation, testing and analysis of cryptographic systems. The role combines mathematics, computer science, algorithms, cybersecurity and probability/statistics.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Sc (General / Honours)","Course":"Statistics & Computer Science / Mathematics & Computing"},"about":[{"label":"Primary Goal","text":"Build mathematics, programming, cybersecurity and cryptographic foundations"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Roadmap Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"A Cryptography Assistant supports the design, implementation, testing and analysis of cryptographic systems. The role combines mathematics, computer science, algorithms, cybersecurity and probability/statistics."},{"type":"p","text":"At undergraduate level, the focus should be on becoming strong in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Number theory and discrete mathematics"},{"text":"Probability and statistics"},{"text":"Algorithms and data structures"},{"text":"Programming"},{"text":"Cryptographic algorithms"},{"text":"Information security"},{"text":"Secure communications"},{"text":"Applied cryptanalysis"},{"text":"Security testing and implementation"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important","text":"A B.Sc alone usually leads to assistant/junior or supporting roles. Dedicated cryptographer, cryptanalyst and cryptographic engineering positions commonly prefer strong postgraduate-level mathematics, computer science, cybersecurity or specialized cryptography knowledge."}]},{"heading":"What to Build During UG","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Learn From","Proof of Skill","Gap to Avoid"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Mathematics + programming"},{"text":"Python, C/C++, discrete mathematics"},{"text":"Programming exercises"},{"text":"Treating cryptography as only encryption/decryption"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Algorithms + number theory"},{"text":"Data structures, modular arithmetic, probability"},{"text":"Algorithm implementations"},{"text":"Weak mathematical foundations"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Cryptography + cybersecurity"},{"text":"Classical and modern cryptography, network security"},{"text":"Cryptography projects"},{"text":"Using cryptographic libraries without understanding concepts"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Applied cryptography + research"},{"text":"PKI, protocols, cryptanalysis, secure systems"},{"text":"Capstone + internship/research"},{"text":"No practical security portfolio"}]]}]},{"heading":"Semester-by-Semester Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Semester 1"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python or C programming"},{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Basic probability"},{"text":"Discrete mathematics"},{"text":"Computer fundamentals"},{"text":"Linux basics"},{"text":"Git/GitHub"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 2"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data structures"},{"text":"Algorithms"},{"text":"Mathematical logic"},{"text":"Combinatorics"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Modular arithmetic"},{"text":"Basic computer networks"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 3"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Number theory"},{"text":"Abstract algebra fundamentals"},{"text":"Probability distributions"},{"text":"Statistical inference"},{"text":"Operating systems"},{"text":"Computer architecture"},{"text":"Python/C++ programming"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 4"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Computer networks"},{"text":"Database fundamentals"},{"text":"Information security"},{"text":"Complexity theory"},{"text":"Algorithms"},{"text":"Cryptography fundamentals"},{"text":"Secure programming"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 5"},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Symmetric cryptography"},{"text":"Public-key cryptography"},{"text":"Hash functions"},{"text":"Digital signatures"},{"text":"Key management"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Random number generation"},{"text":"PKI"},{"text":"Cryptographic protocols"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 6"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cryptanalysis"},{"text":"Applied cryptography"},{"text":"Network security"},{"text":"TLS/HTTPS concepts"},{"text":"Secure communication"},{"text":"Side-channel concepts"},{"text":"Security testing"},{"text":"Cryptographic implementation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 7"},{"type":"h","text":"Choose a specialization:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Applied cryptography"},{"text":"Cryptanalysis"},{"text":"Post-quantum cryptography"},{"text":"Blockchain cryptography"},{"text":"Network security"},{"text":"Cryptographic engineering"},{"text":"Privacy-enhancing technologies"},{"text":"Hardware security"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Semester 8"},{"type":"p","text":"Complete a substantial cryptography/security project and preferably an internship or research project."}]},{"heading":"Core Mathematical Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Cryptography is heavily mathematics-driven."},{"type":"h","text":"Number Theory"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Prime numbers"},{"text":"Divisibility"},{"text":"Euclidean algorithm"},{"text":"Extended Euclidean algorithm"},{"text":"Modular arithmetic"},{"text":"Congruences"},{"text":"Euler's theorem"},{"text":"Fermat's little theorem"},{"text":"Chinese Remainder Theorem"},{"text":"Multiplicative inverses"},{"text":"Discrete logarithms"},{"text":"Finite fields"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Abstract Algebra"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand the concepts behind:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Groups"},{"text":"Rings"},{"text":"Fields"},{"text":"Modular groups"},{"text":"Finite fields"},{"text":"Polynomial arithmetic"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These become particularly useful for understanding modern cryptographic constructions."},{"type":"h","text":"Probability & Statistics"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Probability distributions"},{"text":"Conditional probability"},{"text":"Bayes' theorem"},{"text":"Random variables"},{"text":"Expectation and variance"},{"text":"Statistical inference"},{"text":"Sampling"},{"text":"Hypothesis testing"},{"text":"Entropy concepts"},{"text":"Randomness"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Linear Algebra"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Vectors"},{"text":"Matrices"},{"text":"Linear transformations"},{"text":"Eigenvalues/eigenvectors"},{"text":"Matrix operations"},{"text":"Finite-field linear algebra"}]}]},{"heading":"Cryptography Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Classical Cryptography"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand historically important techniques:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Caesar cipher"},{"text":"Vigenère cipher"},{"text":"Substitution ciphers"},{"text":"Transposition ciphers"},{"text":"Frequency analysis"},{"text":"Classical cryptanalysis"}]},{"type":"p","text":"These are useful for learning cryptographic thinking but are not secure modern systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Symmetric Cryptography"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Block ciphers"},{"text":"Stream ciphers"},{"text":"AES"},{"text":"Modes of operation"},{"text":"CBC"},{"text":"CTR"},{"text":"GCM"},{"text":"Authentication/encryption"},{"text":"Initialization vectors"},{"text":"Nonces"},{"text":"Key management"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Asymmetric Cryptography"},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"RSA"},{"text":"Diffie–Hellman"},{"text":"Elliptic Curve Cryptography"},{"text":"Key exchange"},{"text":"Digital signatures"},{"text":"Public/private keys"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Hash Functions"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SHA-2"},{"text":"SHA-3"},{"text":"Collision resistance"},{"text":"Preimage resistance"},{"text":"Second-preimage resistance"},{"text":"Message authentication codes"},{"text":"HMAC"},{"text":"Password hashing"},{"text":"Key derivation functions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Signatures"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"RSA signatures"},{"text":"ECDSA concepts"},{"text":"EdDSA concepts"},{"text":"Signing/verification"},{"text":"Certificates"},{"text":"Certificate authorities"}]}]},{"heading":"Cryptographic Protocols","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Move beyond individual algorithms and understand how cryptography is used inside systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"TLS/HTTPS"},{"text":"Secure email concepts"},{"text":"VPN cryptography"},{"text":"SSH"},{"text":"PKI"},{"text":"Digital certificates"},{"text":"Authentication protocols"},{"text":"Key exchange"},{"text":"Secure messaging concepts"},{"text":"Password authentication"},{"text":"Token-based authentication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"A major career distinction is:"},{"type":"p","text":"Knowing AES/RSA is not enough. A cryptography professional must understand how cryptographic primitives are securely combined into protocols and systems."}]},{"heading":"Cryptanalysis","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn how cryptographic systems can be evaluated and attacked in controlled environments."},{"type":"h","text":"Topics include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Frequency analysis"},{"text":"Brute-force analysis"},{"text":"Known-plaintext attacks"},{"text":"Chosen-plaintext concepts"},{"text":"Chosen-ciphertext concepts"},{"text":"Differential cryptanalysis concepts"},{"text":"Linear cryptanalysis concepts"},{"text":"Meet-in-the-middle attacks"},{"text":"Weak-key analysis"},{"text":"Randomness testing"},{"text":"Protocol weaknesses"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Also learn the difference between:"},{"type":"p","text":"Breaking an algorithm ≠ exploiting an implementation ≠ exploiting a protocol."}]},{"heading":"Programming Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Primary"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"C/C++"},{"text":"Linux shell"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rust"},{"text":"Java"},{"text":"Go"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Python is particularly useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cryptographic experiments"},{"text":"Number theory"},{"text":"Statistical analysis"},{"text":"Research prototypes"},{"text":"Automation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"C/C++ becomes important when studying:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Performance"},{"text":"Low-level cryptography"},{"text":"Embedded security"},{"text":"Cryptographic libraries"},{"text":"Memory-related vulnerabilities"}]}]},{"heading":"Tools & Technologies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Cryptography"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OpenSSL"},{"text":"OpenSSH"},{"text":"libsodium"},{"text":"PyCryptodome"},{"text":"cryptography (Python)"},{"text":"GnuPG"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Security"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wireshark"},{"text":"Nmap"},{"text":"Burp Suite"},{"text":"OWASP tools"},{"text":"Kali Linux"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Development"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Git"},{"text":"GitHub"},{"text":"VS Code"},{"text":"Linux"},{"text":"Docker"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"SageMath"},{"text":"SymPy"},{"text":"Mathematica concepts"},{"text":"MATLAB"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data Analysis"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"NumPy"},{"text":"pandas"},{"text":"SciPy"},{"text":"matplotlib"},{"text":"Jupyter"}]}]},{"heading":"Projects to Build","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Cryptographic Algorithm Laboratory"},{"type":"h","text":"Implement educational versions of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Caesar cipher"},{"text":"Vigenère cipher"},{"text":"RSA"},{"text":"Diffie–Hellman"},{"text":"AES concepts"},{"text":"SHA hashing concepts"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mathematical explanation"},{"text":"Implementation"},{"text":"Test cases"},{"text":"Security limitations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Secure File Encryption System"},{"type":"h","text":"Build a local application that supports:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Password-based key derivation"},{"text":"Secure encryption"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"File encryption/decryption"},{"text":"Integrity verification"},{"text":"Secure key handling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Use established cryptographic libraries for the actual secure implementation rather than inventing a production cryptographic algorithm."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Cryptanalysis Toolkit"},{"type":"p","text":"Build a research/educational toolkit for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Frequency analysis"},{"text":"Cipher identification"},{"text":"Modular arithmetic"},{"text":"Prime testing"},{"text":"RSA demonstrations"},{"text":"Weak-key demonstrations"},{"text":"Statistical randomness analysis"}]}]},{"heading":"Advanced Capstone Project","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Smart Cryptographic Security Analysis Platform"},{"type":"h","text":"Build a platform that can:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Identify cryptographic algorithms used in a controlled sample."},{"text":"Analyze key sizes and configurations."},{"text":"Detect weak or outdated configurations."},{"text":"Test randomness characteristics."},{"text":"Analyze TLS configurations."},{"text":"Generate security reports."},{"text":"Provide remediation recommendations."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Possible technology stack:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Python","C/C++","OpenSSL","Wireshark","Linux","PostgreSQL","FastAPI","React"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The project should emphasize defensive security and authorized testing."}]},{"heading":"Specialization Choices","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialization","Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Applied Cryptography"},{"text":"Designing and integrating cryptographic systems"}],[{"text":"Cryptanalysis"},{"text":"Studying weaknesses and attacks"}],[{"text":"Cryptographic Engineering"},{"text":"Implementing secure cryptography in software/hardware"}],[{"text":"Network Cryptography"},{"text":"TLS, VPNs, secure communication"}],[{"text":"PKI"},{"text":"Certificates, identity and trust infrastructure"}],[{"text":"Post-Quantum Cryptography"},{"text":"Cryptography resistant to quantum attacks"}],[{"text":"Blockchain Cryptography"},{"text":"Hashing, signatures, consensus-related cryptography"}],[{"text":"Privacy Engineering"},{"text":"Privacy-preserving computation and data protection"}],[{"text":"Hardware Security"},{"text":"Secure processors, HSMs, embedded cryptography"}],[{"text":"Side-Channel Analysis"},{"text":"Timing, power and electromagnetic leakage"}],[{"text":"Applied Mathematics"},{"text":"Mathematical research supporting cryptography"}],[{"text":"Security Research"},{"text":"Vulnerability and protocol research"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internships to Target","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Look for internships in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Information security"},{"text":"Security research"},{"text":"Cryptography research"},{"text":"Network security"},{"text":"Application security"},{"text":"PKI"},{"text":"Identity and access management"},{"text":"Hardware security"},{"text":"Secure software engineering"},{"text":"Security operations"},{"text":"Academic cryptography laboratories"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Good internship outcomes include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Implementing security protocols"},{"text":"Security testing"},{"text":"Cryptographic research"},{"text":"Mathematical modelling"},{"text":"Secure software development"},{"text":"Research papers"},{"text":"Security tools"}]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Certifications are supplementary for cryptography; mathematical and technical depth matters more."},{"type":"h","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cybersecurity fundamentals"},{"text":"Network security"},{"text":"Secure software development"},{"text":"Ethical hacking fundamentals"},{"text":"Cloud security"},{"text":"Applied cryptography"},{"text":"PKI"},{"text":"Linux/security administration"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a cryptography-focused student, university courses, research papers, technical projects and internships can be more valuable than collecting many entry-level certifications."}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"After the B.Sc, realistic adjacent roles include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cryptography Assistant"},{"text":"Junior Cryptography Research Assistant"},{"text":"Security Analyst"},{"text":"Cybersecurity Analyst"},{"text":"Information Security Analyst"},{"text":"Security Operations Analyst"},{"text":"Junior Security Engineer"},{"text":"Application Security Analyst"},{"text":"PKI Support Associate"},{"text":"Identity & Access Management Associate"},{"text":"Secure Software Developer"},{"text":"Research Assistant"},{"text":"Security Testing Associate"},{"text":"Junior Cryptanalysis Researcher"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For dedicated Cryptographer/Cryptanalyst positions, an M.Sc/M.Tech/M.S. or strong research experience can significantly improve competitiveness."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Suitable PG directions include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Mathematics"},{"text":"M.Sc Applied Mathematics"},{"text":"M.Sc Computational Mathematics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Computer Science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Computer Science"},{"text":"M.Sc Computer Science & Applications"},{"text":"M.Tech Computer Science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cybersecurity"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Cybersecurity"},{"text":"M.Tech Cybersecurity"},{"text":"M.Tech Information Security"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Specialized Research"},{"type":"p","text":"Look for programs/research groups involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cryptography"},{"text":"Number theory"},{"text":"Information security"},{"text":"Coding theory"},{"text":"Privacy"},{"text":"Network security"},{"text":"Post-quantum cryptography"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A mathematics-heavy M.Sc can be particularly valuable for someone targeting theoretical cryptography or cryptanalysis."}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Relevant master's programs include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MSc Cryptography"},{"text":"MSc Cybersecurity"},{"text":"MSc Information Security"},{"text":"MSc Computer Science"},{"text":"MSc Mathematics"},{"text":"MSc Applied Mathematics"},{"text":"MSc Security Engineering"},{"text":"MSc Privacy/Security"},{"text":"MSc Post-Quantum Cryptography-related research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Potential destinations:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"USA"},{"text":"UK"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Switzerland"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Singapore"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For research-oriented programs, prioritize faculty research areas and cryptography/security labs rather than choosing solely based on university ranking."}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"B.Sc Statistics & Computer Science / Mathematics & Computing"},{"type":"h","text":"Cryptography/Security Projects"},{"type":"h","text":"Internship / Research Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Cryptography Assistant / Security Analyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Cryptographic Engineer / Security Engineer / Cryptanalyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Cryptography Engineer / Security Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Cryptography Research Lead / Principal Security Engineer"},{"type":"h","text":"Security Architect / Cryptography Architect / Research Scientist"}]},{"heading":"Long-Term Relevance: 2030–2046","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Cryptography is expected to remain strategically important because secure digital communication, identity, financial systems, cloud infrastructure and connected devices require cryptographic protection."},{"type":"h","text":"Important future areas include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Post-Quantum Cryptography"},{"type":"p","text":"Preparing cryptographic systems for adversaries with sufficiently capable quantum computers."},{"type":"h","text":"Privacy-Enhancing Technologies"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Secure multiparty computation"},{"text":"Zero-knowledge proofs"},{"text":"Homomorphic encryption"},{"text":"Privacy-preserving analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"AI + Cryptography"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-assisted cryptanalysis"},{"text":"Automated security analysis"},{"text":"Secure AI systems"},{"text":"Privacy-preserving machine learning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Hardware Security"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Trusted execution environments"},{"text":"Hardware security modules"},{"text":"Secure elements"},{"text":"Embedded cryptography"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Identity"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Digital signatures"},{"text":"Verifiable credentials"},{"text":"Decentralized identity"},{"text":"Certificate infrastructure"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest long-term profile will therefore combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Mathematics","Cryptography","Programming","Cybersecurity","Research","Secure Systems."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Discrete mathematics"},{"text":"Number theory"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Abstract algebra"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Computer Science"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Data structures"},{"text":"Algorithms"},{"text":"Complexity"},{"text":"Operating systems"},{"text":"Computer networks"},{"text":"Secure programming"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Cryptography"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Symmetric cryptography"},{"text":"Public-key cryptography"},{"text":"Hash functions"},{"text":"Digital signatures"},{"text":"PKI"},{"text":"Cryptographic protocols"},{"text":"Cryptanalysis"},{"text":"Post-quantum cryptography"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Python"},{"text":"C/C++"},{"text":"Linux"},{"text":"Git"},{"text":"Rust/Go basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Security"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Network security"},{"text":"Application security"},{"text":"TLS"},{"text":"Authentication"},{"text":"Vulnerability analysis"},{"text":"Secure software development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"OpenSSL"},{"text":"Wireshark"},{"text":"SageMath"},{"text":"SymPy"},{"text":"PyCryptodome"},{"text":"GnuPG"},{"text":"GitHub"}]}]},{"heading":"Final Portfolio Target","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should ideally have:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3–4 cryptography/security projects"},{"text":"1 substantial capstone"},{"text":"Strong number theory and discrete mathematics"},{"text":"Python + C/C++ proficiency"},{"text":"Linux and Git experience"},{"text":"Practical cryptographic implementation knowledge"},{"text":"Cryptanalysis fundamentals"},{"text":"TLS/PKI understanding"},{"text":"1 internship or research experience"},{"text":"Technical documentation/GitHub portfolio"},{"text":"Exposure to post-quantum cryptography"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Graduate Profile"},{"type":"flow","items":["Statistics & Computer Science / Mathematics & Computing","Mathematics","Programming","Algorithms","Cryptography","Cryptanalysis","Cybersecurity","Applied Cryptography","Internship/Research","Cryptography Assistant","Cryptographic Engineer / Security Researcher / Cryptanalyst"]},{"type":"note","label":"Best-fit career cluster","text":"Cybersecurity, Cryptography, Applied Mathematics, Information Security & Security Research."}]}]}